 ### [Raw Volume Data Reader](2259-raw-volume-data-reader.md)
-Ingests raw binary volume data (typically from CT scanners) into memory, applying domain-specific quantization to reduce precision, and preparing the data for GPU transfer. It solves the problem of converting high-precision raw sensor data (e.g., 12-bit Hounsfield units) into a format suitable for real-time raycasting or sparse voxel octree construction, often involving thresholding and bit-depth reduction. It differs from generic loaders by embedding specific quantization logic (scaling and thresholding) directly into the loading pipeline rather than treating data as opaque bytes.
